A = {
210: """The last time I had some real free time was last Sunday. My wife took our daughter to visit her parents for the day, so I had the whole afternoon to myself, which almost never happens. At first, I didn't know what to do. Then I called my best friend, Long, and we decided to go fishing at a small lake outside the city, which we used to do a lot when we were younger. We rode our motorbikes there, rented two fishing rods, and sat by the lake for about three hours. To be honest, we only caught two small fish, but that wasn't important. We talked about everything, from our jobs to our kids to old memories from school. After that, we had some grilled fish and a cold drink at a small restaurant near the lake. It was such a relaxing day, and it reminded me how important it is to have time for friends.""",
211: """People in my country do many different things in their free time. One of the most popular activities is going to coffee shops. Vietnamese people love sitting at a cafe for hours, drinking iced coffee and chatting with friends. It's cheap and relaxing, and it's a big part of our culture. Another popular activity is singing karaoke. Whenever friends or coworkers get together, they often go to a karaoke place or sing at home. What's special about karaoke in Vietnam is that people of all ages enjoy it, from kids to grandparents. Many people also enjoy sports, like football and badminton, and older people often do exercise in parks in the early morning. In recent years, watching videos on social media has become a very common free-time activity too. I think these activities are special because they're usually done together with family and friends, not alone.""",
212: """People in my country have several concerns about holidays. The biggest one is traffic. During long holidays, like Tet or National Day, millions of people travel back to their hometowns or go on vacation at the same time, so the highways and bus stations are extremely crowded. There are also more traffic accidents, especially because some people drink and drive after parties. Another concern is prices. Before and during holidays, prices for food, flights, and hotels go up a lot. Some people also feel stressed, because they have to spend a lot of money on gifts, lucky money, and food. To deal with these issues, the police increase traffic checks and campaigns against drunk driving during holidays. Many people also try to travel earlier or later to avoid the crowds, book tickets far in advance, and plan their budgets carefully before the holiday.""",
213: """I'd like to talk about my best friend, Long. We met in high school, and we've been friends for almost fifteen years now. He's tall and a bit thin, and he always wears glasses. In terms of personality, he's very funny and outgoing. Whenever we have a get-together, he's the one who makes everyone laugh. But what makes him really special to me is that he's very reliable. For example, a few years ago, when my father was in the hospital, Long drove two hours from Hanoi just to bring us food and keep me company, without even telling me he was coming. That really touched me. Now we're both busy with our jobs and families, so we don't meet very often, but we still call each other almost every weekend. I honestly think of him as a member of my family.""",
214: """Last weekend, I spent a lot of time with my family. On Saturday morning, we went to the market together to buy food, because my wife wanted to cook a special lunch. After lunch, we took a nap, and in the late afternoon, we went to the park near our house. My daughter rode her new bicycle, and I ran behind her the whole time, because she's still learning. It was tiring but really fun. In the evening, we watched an animated movie together at home with some popcorn. On Sunday, we visited my parents in my hometown. My mother cooked a big meal, and after lunch, my father and I fixed the fence in their garden while my daughter played with her cousins. Before going home, we all had tea and fruit together in the yard. It was a simple weekend, but I really enjoyed it.""",
215: """A special event I celebrated with my family was my parents' fortieth wedding anniversary last year. My brother and I decided to organize a surprise party for them. We planned it for weeks without telling them. On the day, my brother took my parents out for lunch, while my wife and I decorated their house with flowers, balloons, and old family photos. We also invited our relatives and some of my parents' old friends. When my parents came home in the afternoon, everyone shouted "Surprise!" My mother started crying, and even my father, who rarely shows emotion, looked very touched. Then we had a big dinner together, and my brother and I gave a short speech to thank our parents. Later, we showed a slideshow of their old photos, from their wedding until now. What made it special was seeing how happy and proud they were.""",
216: """Recently, I visited my grandmother in the countryside. It was about a month ago, on a Sunday. She's almost ninety years old and lives with my uncle's family in our home village. When we arrived, she was sitting in the yard, and she was so happy to see us that she held my daughter's hands for a long time. First, we gave her some gifts, like milk, fruit, and a warm blanket. Then my wife helped my aunt cook lunch, while I chatted with my grandmother. She told me stories about my father when he was a little boy, which I had never heard before, and they were really funny. After lunch, my daughter and I fed the chickens in the garden. What was memorable about this visit was that my grandmother taught my daughter a children's song from her childhood. Before we left, she asked us to come back soon.""",
217: """I'd like to talk about my two closest friends, Long and Tuan. Long is my best friend from high school. He's tall, thin, and very outgoing. He loves talking, he's always telling jokes, and he's usually the center of attention at parties. He works in sales, which is perfect for his personality. Tuan, on the other hand, is my friend from university. He's shorter and a bit chubby, and he's much quieter than Long. He's a software engineer, and he's very careful and logical. He's the kind of person who listens more than he talks, and he always gives thoughtful advice. In terms of similarities, both of them are very loyal and kind, and they both love football. They're also both married with young kids, like me. The biggest difference is their personalities. Long is the person I call when I want to have fun, and Tuan is the one I call when I need advice.""",
218: """When I get together with my friends or family, we usually talk about a few main topics. With my friends, since most of us are around thirty and have young children, we often talk about our kids, like their schools, their health, and how to raise them well. We also talk about our jobs and money, for example, salaries, career changes, or investing. Of course, we also talk about football, especially when there's a big match. With my family, the topics are more about family matters, like my parents' health and plans for holidays. These topics are important to us because they're a big part of our daily lives. Sharing experiences helps us learn from each other. For example, my friends have given me useful advice on choosing a kindergarten for my daughter. These conversations also help me feel less stressed, because I know I'm not the only one facing these challenges.""",
219: """In Vietnam, there are many different kinds of hotels, from small, cheap guesthouses to big, luxury five-star hotels. In big cities like Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City, hotels are usually located in the city center, near shopping areas, business districts, or tourist attractions. They're often tall, modern buildings with glass windows, and the expensive ones have swimming pools on the rooftop. In tourist areas like Da Nang or Nha Trang, many hotels and resorts are built along the beach, so guests can enjoy the ocean view from their rooms. These resorts usually have big gardens, outdoor pools, and private beaches. In smaller towns, there are mostly small family-run hotels and guesthouses, which are simple but clean and cheap. Recently, homestays have also become very popular, especially in mountain areas like Sa Pa, where tourists can stay with local families and experience their culture.""",
220: """I usually stay at hotels when I go on vacation with my family or when I go on business trips. When I arrive at a hotel, the first thing I do is check in at the reception desk. I show my ID card and confirm my booking, and the receptionist gives me the room key and tells me the breakfast time and the Wi-Fi password. Then I go up to my room. The first thing I do in the room is check everything, like the air conditioner, the bathroom, and the bed, to make sure everything is clean and working. Then I unpack my bags and take a shower to refresh myself after the trip. If it's a vacation, we usually rest for a little while and then go out to explore the area or go to the beach. On the last day, I pack carefully and check out before noon.""",
221: """The hotel I remember the most is a small resort in Phu Quoc, an island in the south of Vietnam. I stayed there with my wife for our honeymoon about seven years ago. It was located right on the beach, a bit far from the busy town center, so it was very quiet and peaceful. The resort had small private bungalows made of wood with thatched roofs, surrounded by palm trees and tropical flowers. Our bungalow had a big glass door that opened directly onto the beach, so in the morning, we could walk from our bed to the sea in just a minute. The staff were incredibly friendly, and on our first night, they surprised us with a candlelight dinner on the beach because they knew it was our honeymoon. It was memorable because of the beautiful view, the amazing service, and of course, because it was a very special time in our lives.""",
222: """The last time I stayed at a hotel was about three months ago, when I went to Ho Chi Minh City for a business trip. I had to attend a three-day training course at our company's office there. I stayed at a business hotel near the city center, which my company had booked for me. When I arrived on the first evening, I checked in, went to my room, and had a quick dinner at a restaurant nearby. The room was small but clean and modern, with a big window that looked over the busy street. For the next three days, I had breakfast at the hotel every morning, took a taxi to the training, and came back in the evening. On the second evening, some coworkers from the southern office took me out to try local food, which was a lot of fun. On the last day, I checked out early and flew back home.""",
223: """To be honest, I don't read paper newspapers anymore. I read the news online every day, usually on my phone. My routine is quite simple. In the morning, while I'm having breakfast or drinking coffee, I open a news app or website and spend about fifteen minutes reading. Sometimes I also read in the evening, after my daughter goes to sleep, while I'm lying on the sofa. When I choose what to read first, I usually start with the headlines on the front page to see what the most important news of the day is. Then I read the sections that I'm interested in, like technology, business, and sports. I usually skip celebrity news. If there's something interesting or important, I read the whole article, but most of the time, I just read the titles and the first few lines. On weekends, I also read some longer articles in English to practice.""",
224: """I first became interested in reading newspapers when I was in high school. My father used to buy a newspaper every morning, and after he finished, he left it on the table. At first, I only read the sports section, because I loved football and wanted to read about the matches. Then I started reading other sections too, like news about science and technology, because I found them interesting. My father noticed and often discussed the news with me during dinner, which made me feel more grown-up. When I went to university, I started reading news online, because it was faster and free. Over the years, my interests have changed. Now I read more about the economy and technology, because they're related to my job. I also try to read some English news websites to improve my English. So my interest has grown, but the way I read news has completely changed.""",
225: """In my country, there are many kinds of newspapers, both printed and online. Some are national newspapers that report on news from all over the country, and others are local newspapers that focus on news from a specific city or province. There are also specialized newspapers about topics like sports, business, law, or young people. These days, most newspapers have online versions, and some news websites are only online. They typically report on current events, like politics, the economy, traffic, weather, and social issues. A typical newspaper has several sections. For example, there's a section for national news, international news, business, technology, health, education, sports, and entertainment. Many online newspapers also have sections for travel, food, and lifestyle, and they often include videos and photos. Some newspapers are also published in English for foreigners living in Vietnam.""",
226: """One news story that really interested me was about a group of young engineers in Vietnam who built a low-cost robot to help clean up trash in rivers. I read it on a news website about a year ago. The article explained that the robot could float on the water and collect plastic bottles and bags automatically, and it was much cheaper than similar machines from other countries. They tested it on a polluted river in Hanoi, and it worked quite well. What made this story more memorable than other news was that it was positive and inspiring. Most news about the environment is depressing, but this one showed that young Vietnamese people can use technology to solve real problems. After reading it, I felt proud and hopeful. It also made me think about how I could teach my daughter to care about the environment from a young age.""",
227: """Newspapers today are very different from those in the past. In the past, most people read printed newspapers that were published once a day. People usually bought them from newsstands in the morning, and the news was often from the day before. The articles were mostly long texts with a few black-and-white photos. Today, most people read news online, and it's updated every minute, so we can know what's happening almost instantly. The way news is reported has also changed a lot. Online articles are shorter and include lots of photos, videos, and even live updates. Many newspapers also share their news on social media, and readers can comment and share articles right away. However, there are some problems too. Because news needs to be fast, sometimes it's less accurate, and there's a lot of fake news on social media, so readers need to be more careful.""",
228: """Newspapers are definitely moving from paper to digital formats, and this change has affected how people get their news in many ways. First, news is much faster and easier to access now. People can read the news on their phones anytime and anywhere, like on the bus or during a lunch break, and they don't need to buy a newspaper. Second, digital news is more interactive. Articles often include videos, maps, and links to related stories, and readers can leave comments and share them with friends. Third, many people now get news from social media rather than directly from newspaper websites, which means they often only read headlines. On the negative side, many printed newspapers have lost readers and money, and some have had to close. Also, it's harder to tell what's true online. Personally, I like digital news, but I try to read from reliable sources.""",
229: """I like watching a few kinds of TV programs. My favorite type is football. I'm a big fan of the English Premier League, so I watch matches on weekends whenever I can, especially late at night. Watching football helps me relax and forget about work, and it's exciting because you never know what will happen. I also like watching documentaries about nature and science. They're really interesting, and I learn a lot about the world, like how animals live or how things are made. Sometimes I watch them with my daughter, and she asks me lots of questions. Besides that, my wife and I enjoy watching Korean dramas together in the evening. At first, I only watched them because of my wife, but now I'm hooked too, because the stories are emotional and the actors are very good. These programs give me different things: excitement, knowledge, and relaxation.""",
230: """I watch TV most often in the evening, after dinner, from around eight to ten o'clock. On weekends, I sometimes stay up late to watch football matches. I usually watch TV in the living room, because that's where our big smart TV is. Most of the time, I watch with my wife after our daughter goes to bed, and we usually watch a drama series or a movie together. Earlier in the evening, I sometimes watch cartoons with my daughter, because she loves them. While watching TV, I usually do other things at the same time. For example, I might eat fruit or snacks, fold the laundry, or check my phone. When I watch football with my friends, we usually drink some beer and shout at the TV. To be honest, I don't watch traditional TV channels very much anymore. I mostly watch programs on streaming apps through the smart TV.""",
231: """When I was young, TV programs were very different from now. There were only a few channels, and most of them were national channels. The programs were mainly news, documentaries, music shows, and Vietnamese or Chinese drama series. There weren't many programs for kids, so I remember waiting all week for a cartoon that was only shown on Sunday mornings. Also, TV programs were only shown at specific times, so if you missed an episode, you couldn't watch it again. Today, things have changed completely. There are hundreds of channels and streaming apps, so people can choose from thousands of programs, including movies, shows, and cartoons from all over the world. People can watch anything at any time, and even pause or rewind. Another big change is reality shows and game shows, which are very popular now. The quality of the programs is also much better, with high-definition images.""",
232: """I first became interested in watching TV when I was about six years old. My family had a small black-and-white TV, and in the evening, my neighbors often came over to watch it with us, because not every family had one. When I was a child, I loved watching cartoons, especially Japanese cartoons like Doraemon, which were on TV every week. I also liked watching a children's quiz show and Chinese kung fu dramas with my father. As I got older, my interests changed. In high school, I started watching football matches and music shows with my friends. After I started working, I didn't have much time for TV, so I mostly watched the news in the evening. These days, I watch TV with my family. I watch cartoons with my daughter and dramas with my wife, so in a way, my interests have come back to where they started.""",
233: """One of the rising industries in my country is the electronics manufacturing industry. Over the past ten to fifteen years, Vietnam has become one of the biggest producers of electronics in the world, especially smartphones, laptops, and electronic components. This industry is famous because many big international companies from Korea, Japan, and the US have built huge factories in Vietnam. What's special about it is how fast it has grown. Electronics are now among Vietnam's biggest exports, and they bring in a lot of money for the country. Another special thing is that it creates hundreds of thousands of jobs, especially in provinces near Hanoi, like Bac Ninh and Thai Nguyen, where I live. Recently, the industry has been moving into more advanced areas, like semiconductor chips, which many people think will be very important for Vietnam's future.""",
234: """I'd like to talk about a large Korean electronics company that has many factories in Vietnam. It's one of the biggest technology companies in the world, and it makes smartphones, TVs, home appliances, and computer chips. What's special about this company in Vietnam is the size of its investment. It started building factories here about fifteen years ago, and now it's one of the biggest foreign investors in the country. Its factories in Vietnam produce a large share of its smartphones sold around the world. Another special thing is that it employs a huge number of Vietnamese workers and engineers, and it also trains them and works with local suppliers. In my area, this company has really changed the local economy. Many people have stable jobs, and there are new apartments, shops, and schools around the industrial parks. Many young people dream of working there.""",
235: """The electronics industry brings many benefits to my country. The first and most obvious benefit is jobs. Big factories employ hundreds of thousands of workers, so many young people, especially from rural areas, have stable jobs with good salaries and insurance. This helps families improve their lives. The second benefit is for the economy. Electronics are among Vietnam's biggest exports, so they bring a lot of money into the country and help the economy grow. Third, the industry helps develop local areas. Around industrial parks, there are new roads, apartments, shopping centers, and schools, which improve people's quality of life. Another important benefit is skills and technology. Vietnamese workers and engineers learn modern technology and management skills from foreign companies, and some local companies have become suppliers for these big companies. In the long term, I think this will help Vietnam develop its own technology industry.""",
236: """In my country, many young people want to work for big multinational companies, especially in technology and manufacturing. They're attracted by the good salaries, benefits like health insurance and bonuses, and a professional working environment. These companies also offer training programs and chances to work abroad, which is very attractive. Another popular choice is big technology companies and startups, especially in software and e-commerce. Young people like them because the work is modern, the culture is often relaxed, and they can learn new skills quickly. Some young people also want to work for banks or government agencies, because these jobs are stable and respected by their parents. Recently, more young people are also interested in starting their own business or working as freelancers, like content creators on social media, because they want more freedom and flexibility. I think young people today care about both salary and personal growth.""",
237: """I remember an incident in the smartphone industry a few years ago. A famous phone brand released a new model that was highly advertised. Before the launch, there was a lot of excitement, and many people in my community, especially young people, were waiting to buy it. However, after it was released, many users started complaining online. The phone got very hot when people played games or used the camera for a long time, and the battery drained quickly. Some people even posted videos showing the problem. The reaction in my community was quite strong. Many people who had pre-ordered the phone canceled their orders, and some people who had already bought it tried to return it. On social media, there were lots of jokes and negative comments. Later, the company released a software update to fix the problem, but many people had already lost trust and decided to wait for the next model.""",
238: """In my country, people prepare for future work in different ways. Most people first get a general education, finishing high school and then going to university or college. At university, they study a major, like engineering, business, or IT, but many people say that what they learn is too theoretical. So once they join a company, they usually receive specific training. For example, big companies have training programs for new employees to teach them about their products and processes. Young people don't usually get specific job training from a very young age, except for some vocational schools. Over the past five years, the process has changed quite a lot. More students now do internships while they're still at university to gain real experience. Many people also take online courses to learn practical skills, like coding, English, or data analysis. Also, companies are working more closely with universities to train students.""",
239: """I exchange text messages with my friends almost every day, but they're usually short and casual. Most of my messages are about making plans, like arranging when and where to meet for coffee or football. We also have a group chat with my high school friends, and we send funny pictures, videos, and jokes there to make each other laugh. Sometimes we discuss news or football matches, especially after a big game. With my close friends, I also send messages to ask how they're doing or to share good news, like when my daughter won a prize at kindergarten. On special occasions, like birthdays or Tet, I send messages with best wishes. I usually use messaging apps rather than normal text messages, because I can send photos, voice messages, and stickers for free. I rarely send long messages, though. If something is important, I prefer to call.""",
}
